//@version=6
indicator("Printer — Bar Reporter", overlay = true)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHY THIS EXISTS
// The server has no price feed by design — it only knows what webhooks tell
// it. Zone geometry arrives from "Printer — StatMap Zone Publisher" (4H
// chart), but detecting when price TAPS a zone needs bar-by-bar prices. This
// heartbeat supplies them: one JSON webhook per 1-minute bar close, carrying
// the bar's OHLC. The server does the tap detection itself — in testable
// Python, not Pine.
//
// It doubles as the server's wall clock: validity windows and expiries can
// tick off received bars instead of trusting local time.
//
// RUN THIS ON THE NQ1! CONTINUOUS 1-MINUTE CHART — the same symbol the Zone
// Publisher computes from, so tap comparisons are apples to apples.
//
// It has NO inputs, so the alert is created once and NEVER needs re-creating.
// Fires once per bar close — the project's standard alert cadence.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

f_price_string(_price) =>
    str.tostring(_price, format.mintick)

bar_payload = '{"indicator":"BARS","event":"bar_close"' +
     ',"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '"' +
     ',"chart_timeframe":"' + timeframe.period + '"' +
     ',"open":"' + f_price_string(open) + '"' +
     ',"high":"' + f_price_string(high) + '"' +
     ',"low":"' + f_price_string(low) + '"' +
     ',"close":"' + f_price_string(close) + '"' +
     ',"bar_close_time_ny":"' + str.format_time(time_close, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss", "America/New_York") + '"}'

// Unconditional call: the once-per-bar-close frequency makes this fire exactly
// once per completed realtime bar and never on historical bars.
alert(bar_payload, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
